# These files run inside Linux containers — always check out with LF endings,
# even on Windows, so shell scripts and configs don't break with CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.env text eol=lf
*.env.example text eol=lf

# PRIVATE — must NOT ship in the public open-source snapshot. `export-ignore` drops
# these from `git archive`; whoever cuts the release must also exclude them if using
# any other mechanism. The authoritative rationale (belongs / excluded / scrub-first)
# is docs/open-source-manifest.md (§B). Keep this list in sync with it.

# -- Live provisioning/credential runbooks --
docs/web-app-chat-provisioning.md export-ignore
docs/todo-24-secrets-resync-runbook.md export-ignore

# -- Internal ops + working notes (backlog, weekly reviews, agent notes) --
# todos.md exposes the private product portfolio + live provisioning state; it was
# shipping in the archive until 2026-07-22. The manifest describes the exclusion
# strategy itself; CLAUDE.md is internal working notes (IPs/hosts/sibling repos).
todos.md export-ignore
docs/open-source-manifest.md export-ignore
docs/Week 1 - 2026-06-15 - Week In Review.md export-ignore
CLAUDE.md export-ignore

